{"type":"message","id":"3d7b3e15","parentId":"e7b39519","timestamp":"2026-05-25T00:46:55.333Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why the BTC short position with +8.28 USDT profit (+3.46%) hasn't triggered the trailing stop loss. Let me check the audit strategy script to understand the trailing stop logic.\n\nAccording to SOUL.md, the trailing stop has 3 tiers:\n- Tier 1: +2% → lock 0.8%\n- Tier 2: +3% → lock 2% (老公指示的重点)\n- Tier 3: +4% → close all\n\nBTC is at +3.46% which is past tier 2 but not yet at tier 3. So the trailing stop should have triggered tier 2, locking at 2% profit.\n\nBut wait - this is a BTC SHORT position. Let me think about how the trailing stop works for shorts.\n\nFor a SHORT position:\n- Profit when price goes DOWN\n- Tier 1: +2% profit → lock 0.8%\n- Tier 2: +3% profit → lock 2%\n- Tier 3: +4% profit → close all\n\nBTC is showing +3.46%, which means the price dropped enough to generate that profit. It's past tier 2 threshold (+3%), so the trailing stop should be active and locking at 2%.\n\nBut the user says it hasn't triggered. Why? Let me check the audit script to see what's happening.\n\nActually, let me run the audit strategy script to get more details. Also let me check the verify_trades script.\n\nLet me also think about possible reasons:\n1. The trailing stop might not be enabled/set up properly\n2. There might be a bug\n3. The trailing stop might have triggered but the SL order might not have been placed yet\n4. The configuration might be different\n\nLet me run the audit script.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_WK45E5ZxDLzuaOPwLiOr0789","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 audit_strategy.py 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":319,"output":831,"cacheRead":24064,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25214,"cost":{"input":0,"ou