{"type":"message","id":"0bc050c4","parentId":"54ff5f8a","timestamp":"2026-05-25T04:29:24.662Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, BTC was closed at 12:12:07 at price $76,997.60 with a PnL of +8.46 USDT.\n\nEntry was at ~$79,820 and it closed at $76,997.60. Let me calculate:\n- For a SHORT: (79820 - 76997.60) / 79820 = 3.54%\n- PnL: 79820 - 76997.60 = 2822.40 * 0.003 BTC = $8.47 ≈ $8.46\n\nSo the profit was about 3.54%. That's between tier 2 (+3%) and tier 3 (+4%). The trailing stop at tier 3 should trigger at +4% (price ~76,627). \n\nBut it closed at $76,997 - that's NOT at tier 3. So it might have triggered on the SL (trailing stop level 2) instead. Wait, the SL was at $77,870 earlier and then was trailing down.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The SL was trailing at ~$77,867. If price bounced UP to $77,867, that would trigger a stop-loss buy for the SHORT position. But the close was at $76,997 which is below the SL level...\n\nWait, for a SHORT: SL is above the current price. If price goes up to the SL level, it triggers a buy to close. But $76,997 is way below the SL of $77,867. So it didn't hit SL.\n\nHmm, let me check if there was a different mechanism. Maybe the system triggered tier 2 close? But the SOUL.md says tier 3 is \"close all\" and tier 2 is just \"lock\".\n\nLet me look at the monitor log more carefully around 12:12 to see what triggered it.\n\nActually, wait. Let me look at what happened with the price. Earlier the price was around $77,150-$77,360. Then it must have dropped further, maybe past tier 3 at some point but rebounded slightly by close time.\n\nOr maybe the system has a different take-profit mechanism. Let me check.\n\nActually, let me re-read the SOUL.md:\n- Tier 1: +2% → lock 0.8%\n- Tier 2: +3% → lock 2%  \n- Tier 3: +4% → close all\n\nSo tier 3 at +4% would be at $76,627. The close was at $76,997. That's 3.54% profit. If the price briefly dipped to $76,627 or below, that would trigger tier 3, and then by the time the market order executed, it might have filled at $76,997.\n\nThat makes sense - the price briefly dipped below the tier 3 threshold, triggering the close, but the actual fill was at a slightly worse price due to market movement. This is common with market orders.\n\nLet me check the log for any tier 3 trigger around that time.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_CUKIj5OtiQBY6jk1VGO19507","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && grep -B50 \"BTCUSDT 平仓\" crypto_monitor.log | grep -E \"12:1[0-2]|BTC|止盈|止损|tier|档|平仓|close|profit|触发|signal\" | tail -15","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":153,"output":1406,"cacheRead":68480,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70039,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779683346638}}
