{"type":"message","id":"e264a992","parentId":"1ffdfd62","timestamp":"2026-05-25T04:31:21.896Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fd link says the monitor is logging to `/root/.openclaw/logs/trading/archive/legacy_trading_20` but that file doesn't exist now. The monitor must have rotated the log.\n\nOK, let me take a different approach. The verify_trades showed:\n- BTC closed at 12:12:07 at $76,997.60 with PnL of +8.46 USDT\n- Entry was ~$79,820\n\nProfit = (79820 - 76997.60) / 79820 = 3.54%\n\nThe tier 3 (close all) triggers at +4%, which would be $76,627. The close was at $76,997.\n\nPossible explanations:\n1. The price briefly touched $76,627 or below (tier 3), triggered the close, but the actual fill was at $76,997 due to slippage on a market order\n2. There's a different mechanism - maybe the monitor detected peak profit had reached +4% but pulled back, triggering the trailing stop\n3. It was a manual close\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-check the SOUL.md trailing stop mechanism:\n- Peak profit tracking: when price moves favorably, it tracks the peak. If price pulls back, it triggers the trailing stop at the appropriate lock level.\n\nIf BTC was a SHORT at entry $79,820:\n- Price dropped to below $76,627 → peak profit >4% → tier 3 triggered\n- But by the time the order executed, price rebounded to $76,997 → filled at a worse price\n- PnL at fill: (79820-76997.6)/79820 = 3.54%\n\nThis is the most likely scenario. Let me also check the current position to see if BTC is gone (which would confirm it was fully closed).\n\nActually, let me also look for the monitor's actual log output to confirm the trigger.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rZFxmMptnw4IQt34VHNd9715","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 query_positions.py 2>&1 | grep \"BTC\\|持仓\"","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage"