{"type":"message","id":"2a7fe314","parentId":"d870e4c1","timestamp":"2026-05-25T14:17:44.565Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why \"today's realized\" shows 0 when BTC was closed today. I already explained this earlier but let me be more precise.\n\nLooking at the data:\n- BTC SHORT was closed at 12:12:07, PnL +8.46 USDT (confirmed by verify_trades)\n- The monitor restarted at 10:09, which reset `daily_pnl` to 0\n- The query_positions.py reads daily_pnl from crypto_state.json\n- After the restart, the daily_pnl was set to 0 and the BTC close at 12:12 should have added to it\n\nBut wait, if the monitor was restarted and the daily_pnl was reset, then the BTC close should have been recorded in the new session. Unless...\n\nLet me check the crypto_state.json to see what daily_pnl says.\n\nActually, the issue might be more nuanced. The `daily_pnl` in crypto_state.json is maintained by the running monitor process. When it restarts at 10:09, it resets to 0. The BTC close at 12:12 should have been tracked by the running monitor and added to daily_pnl. But if there was another restart between then and now...\n\nActually, let me just check the current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_T0lCq44cHWLIVsx1xRpA8985","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('crypto_state.json'))\nprint('daily_pnl:', s.get('daily_pnl'))\nprint('peak_pnl_map:', json.dumps(s.get('peak_pnl_map',{}), indent=2))\n\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":407,"output":667,"cacheRead":75392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76466,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779718656051}}
